cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata below.

title: >-
  DonatJS Core: A Zero-Dependency JSON-Driven Client-Side Router
  and UI Rendering Engine

abstract: >-
  DonatJS Core (script.js) is a zero-dependency, no-build-step client-side
  rendering (CSR) engine that transforms structured data (JSON) into dynamic
  web interfaces through a polymorphic component dispatch system. Developed at
  Sismadi Lab (sismadi.com) — Experimental Zone, where Frameworks Are Born
  Before Becoming Products — owned by PT Sismadi Langit Solusi. DonatJS is
  the third generation of the framework lineage born at the same lab:
  Ktupad (2019, EC00201952487) → BayamJS (2023, EC00202367008) →
  DonatJS (2024, EC00202414144), all registered as official copyrights at
  DJKI (Direktorat Jenderal Kekayaan Intelektual), Republic of Indonesia.
  The architecture rests on three pillars: (1) Micro Routing System based on
  query strings with History API and automatic fallback resolution;
  (2) JSON-Driven Component Architecture where all layouts and content are
  defined as flat JavaScript objects (pages.*) without explicit HTML markup;
  (3) Polymorphic Render Engine that dispatches component functions
  (components[section]) based on the section field in data. Built-in
  components include hero, features, article, titleHero, learningModule
  (with navigation sidebar), quizEngine (base64-protected), certificate
  (printable), slideViewer (PREP-structured), and live dataset editor.
  A Markdown-like lineRenderer supports code blocks, headings, skill bars,
  timeline steps, inline tables, and form validation. SVG.js integrates
  via svg.di(), executed automatically on every route navigation.
  Patent application: S00202503129 (DJKI).

